From 062f249f6e8bb84d03be6e2583e9656b32ddcfab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 07:50:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a setting for HDR at more than 8 bits where
 the graphics send RGB at 8 bits at most

Over HDMI, driver 580 sends RGB at 8 bits at most on GeForce GTX 10 cards
and the TITAN V, and driver 615 does on GeForce GTX 16 and RTX 20
graphics, whatever the TV takes. Each driver has a parameter of
nvidia-modeset that sends HDR deeper there, off by default:
hades_hdr_ycbcr422 (driver 580: YCbCr 4:2:2 at 10 bits) and
hades_turing_12bpc (driver 615: 12 bits where the mode fits).

System > Display > "HDR at more than 8 bits where the card sends RGB at 8
(NVIDIA)", shown where the driver has one of them that can be written,
writes them before the mode set of each HDR video (HdrMoreBits.h), so it
applies from the next video and needs no kernel parameter. Off by
default. Graphics that send RGB at more than 8 bits are not touched: the
driver checks it. kodi.log says each change.
