+
+#. Hades: label of the setting of HDR at more than 8 bits where the graphics send RGB at 8 bits at most (NVIDIA)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#41011"
+msgid "HDR at more than 8 bits where the card sends RGB at 8 (NVIDIA)"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: help of the setting of HDR at more than 8 bits where the graphics send RGB at 8 bits at most
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#41012"
+msgid "For NVIDIA graphics that send RGB at 8 bits at most over HDMI, whatever the TV takes. On GeForce GTX 10 cards and the TITAN V, HDR goes out in YCbCr 4:2:2 at 10 bits; on GeForce GTX 16 and RTX 20 graphics, at 12 bits where the mode fits (3840x2160 up to 30 Hz on HDMI 2.0). Where the TV or the mode does not take it, HDR goes out as before. Dolby Vision and SDR are not affected, nor graphics that send RGB at more than 8 bits. Off until it is confirmed on those cards. Applies from the next video."
+msgstr ""
